# Baseline for <COPILOT_HOME>/tool-permissions (~/.copilot by default, ~/.config/copilot-<name> for `copilot -u <name>`).
# Copy by hand. plugins/30-copilot.sh turns each `allow <pattern>` / `deny <pattern>` line into a
# --allow-tool= / --deny-tool= flag on every `copilot` invocation; `#` comments and blank lines are ignored.
#
# The allow rules between the GENERATED markers come from the shared tier of config/agents/shell-permissions.jsonc; edit
# that list and run `config/agents/sync.ts generate` (see config/copilot/README.md). Copilot matches shell rules on a
# command identifier (the command name, plus a first-level subcommand for tools such as git, gh, npm), never on the full
# command text, so only entries whose identifier is no broader than the glob are emitted. Commands copilot's built-in
# read-only tier already auto-approves (cat, grep, ls, git status, gh pr view, ...) are left out. Everything else keeps
# asking.

# BEGIN GENERATED shell-permissions (config/agents/sync.ts generate); do not edit by hand
allow shell(ag:*)
allow shell(b2sum:*)
allow shell(base64:*)
allow shell(basename:*)
allow shell(bat:*)
allow shell(cd:*)
allow shell(cksum:*)
allow shell(cmp:*)
allow shell(column:*)
allow shell(comm:*)
allow shell(dirname:*)
allow shell(dirs:*)
allow shell(egrep:*)
allow shell(fgrep:*)
allow shell(fmt:*)
allow shell(fold:*)
allow shell(gh browse:*)
allow shell(git cat-file:*)
allow shell(git ls-tree:*)
allow shell(git reflog:*)
allow shell(git rev-list:*)
allow shell(hexdump:*)
allow shell(join:*)
allow shell(jq:*)
allow shell(locate:*)
allow shell(md5sum:*)
allow shell(npm --version)
allow shell(npm -v)
allow shell(npm info:*)
allow shell(npm list:*)
allow shell(npm ls:*)
allow shell(npm outdated:*)
allow shell(npm view:*)
allow shell(npx --version)
allow shell(od:*)
allow shell(paste:*)
allow shell(pnpm --version)
allow shell(pnpm list:*)
allow shell(pnpm why:*)
allow shell(popd:*)
allow shell(printf:*)
allow shell(pushd:*)
allow shell(sha1sum:*)
allow shell(sha256sum:*)
allow shell(sha512sum:*)
allow shell(shasum:*)
allow shell(shopt:*)
allow shell(tac:*)
allow shell(test:*)
allow shell(tree:*)
allow shell(xxd:*)
allow shell(yamllint:*)
allow shell(yarn --version)
allow shell(yarn list:*)
allow shell(yarn why:*)
# END GENERATED shell-permissions

# Secrets: mirrors Claude's Read(./.env*) denies. Covers copilot's file tools only; shell reads such as `cat .env` go
# through the read-only tier, the same gap Claude has with Bash(cat *).
deny read(.env)
deny read(.env.*)
deny read(.envrc)
